    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Factorise 2015",
        "body": "$2015 = 5 \\cdot 13 \\cdot 31$, so the factor pairs are $1 \\cdot 2015$, $5 \\cdot 403$, $13 \\cdot 155$ and $31 \\cdot 65$. Nobody is 155, 403 or 2015 years old, so the father is 65 and the son 31. The difference is $65 - 31 = 34$.\n\n(Of the listed differences only 34 occurs at all: the four pairs have differences 2014, 398, 142 and 34.)\n\n**Answer: (D) 34**"
      }
    ],
