        "title": "Use the 'mixed' label",
        "body": "Take one candy from the dispenser labelled \"mixed\". Its label is wrong, so it contains only one flavour — the flavour of the candy he got, say cherry. Now the dispenser labelled \"lemon\" is not lemon (wrong label) and not cherry (that one is found), so it is mixed. The last dispenser is lemon.\n\nZero candies cannot be enough: there are two ways to derange three labels, and without any information Robert cannot tell them apart. So the minimum is 1.\n\n**Answer: (A) 1**"
