    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Complementary key sets",
        "body": "Each director holds a 3-element subset of the 6 locks' keys. Two directors together can open the safe exactly when their two sets together contain all 6 keys, i.e. when one set is the **complement** of the other.\n\nThere are $\\binom63 = 20$ possible key sets, and they split into $10$ complementary pairs. From each pair at most one set may be used, so there are at most 10 directors; choosing one set from every pair gives 10 directors, no two of which can open the safe.\n\n**Answer: (C) 10**"
      }
    ],
